==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|а́ккула}} {{lb|ru|dialectal}}

===Etymology===
Directly attested since 18th century as {{m|ru|а́ккула}} and {{m|ru|акул}}, while derivative {{m|ru|акулий}} is used to describe liver oil of a [[Greenland shark]] in a source going back to late 16th or early 17th century.

Immediate borrowing from rather different {{der|ru|non|hákarl}} (see internal etymology there) is rejected by Anikin, he rather proposes mediation by some {{bor|ru|smi}} language.

Compare dialectal {{cog|no|haakall}}, {{cog|sms|akkli}}, {{cog|sjd|а̄һклэӈӈк}}, {{cog|se|áhkạlakkis|t=Greenland shark}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|аку́ла}}
* {{audio|Ru-акула.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|аку́ла|a=an}}

# [[shark]]

